		(property "Winding" "Do Not Twist Tightly: If you twist the wires into a tight rope, the diameter increases, and it won't fit through the hole 3 times.  \"Parallel Lay\": Keep the wires mostly parallel (untwisted) inside the hole. Let them nest against each other. Twist them slightly outside the loop (at the top/bottom) to keep them paired, but let them lay flat like ribbons inside the ferrite.  Lube: A tiny drop of isopropyl alcohol can help the Teflon-coated wires slide over each other for the final turn without tearing the insulation."
